        {
          "platform": "x",
          "url": "https://x.com/AnthropicAI/status/2113390212911083894",
          "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T22:01:06Z",
          "retrievedAt": null
        },
        {
          "platform": "github",
          "url": "https://github.com/theorem-labs/oss-verify-proofs",
          "publishedAt": "2026-10-22T17:20:28Z",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-24T01:11:13+08:00"
        }
      ],
      "repository": {
        "language": "Rocq Prover",
        "stars": 80,
        "license": "MIT",
        "commit": "8f5f4676"
      },
      "scores": {
        "breakthrough": 90,
        "interestingness": 92,
        "technicalDepth": 92,
        "reproducibility": 82,
        "credibility": 92
      },
      "eligibility": "eligible",
      "reason": "Weighted 89.9 >= 80. Verified against primary sources: Anthropic research post read in full (published Oct 22, 2026, Frontier Red Team with Theorem; 239 entry points across 123 OSS-Fuzz libraries proved crash-free for every input under 64 MB on compiled RISC-V binaries; about 180 million lines of Rocq, typical proof about 600,000 lines, median binary 18,000 RISC-V instructions; trusted base is the RISC-V and Linux-process semantics, the theorem statements and the Rocq checker; bugs found include a 20 MB-input decompressor out-of-bounds write and a rediscovery of CVE-2026-56132 in libexpat; Opus 5.5 proves half of 36 tasks with about 40% fewer tokens than Opus 5; shared proof workspace cut tokens 17%; limitations: single-threaded static RISC-V/musl only, ASan does not catch all memory bugs, proofs cost hundreds of millions of tokens). Official @AnthropicAI post 22:01:06Z. GitHub theorem-labs/oss-verify-proofs (MIT, created 2026-10-22T17:20:28Z, release commit 8f5f4676 \"OSS Verify proofs 2026.10.0\" at 20:28:58Z) README read: the public subset covers 60 entry points in 25 libraries, checked with Rocq 9.2.0 in the LPS Linux-process model, which the README calls best effort and not complete. AgentLab did not re-check the proofs (codeStatus not_run)."
    },
